cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "gdgap: gender-blind vs. gender-aware data warehousing over the 2017 NHTS"
authors:
  - family-names: "Torda"
    given-names: "Balázs"
    email: "balazs.torda@iu-study.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jurdabos/gdgap"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - "gender data gap"
  - "sex-disaggregated data"
  - "data warehousing"
  - "data quality"
  - "DuckDB"
  - "DuckLake"
  - "NHTS 2017"
abstract: >-
  Design-science artefact contrasting a gender-blind and a gender-aware warehouse
  variant built from the identical 2017 NHTS source: sex/gender as a first-class,
  provenance-carrying dimension with validity-interval mutability handling, derived
  equity measures (care-trip share, PPR) under small-cell suppression, an executable
  data-quality contract, and a benchmark harness against a containerised InnoDB foil.
